# Never commit a raw activity file. Garmin exports carry the owner's name, a
# biometric profile, the watch serial number and the exact date of the session.
# The only .fit files allowed in this repo are the scrubbed test fixtures --
# see AGENTS.md and tools/scrub-fixtures.mjs.
# Case-folded on purpose: Garmin writes GARMIN/ACTIVITY/*.FIT in uppercase on
# the watch itself, and a plain `*.fit` misses it on any case-sensitive
# filesystem -- which is every Linux box and every CI runner. macOS hides the
# bug locally because core.ignorecase defaults to true there.
*.[Ff][Ii][Tt]
# `**` so fixtures can be organised into subdirectories later; `*` does not
# cross a `/`, so `fixtures/forerunner265/x.fit` would otherwise be invisible
# to git and fail in CI with a confusing ENOENT.
!packages/fitfix/test/fixtures/**/*.[Ff][Ii][Tt]
!packages/fitfix/test/fixtures/*.[Ff][Ii][Tt]

# Your own name, watch serial and sensor ids, for the text cross-check in
# tools/scrub-fixtures.mjs. Committing these would make the privacy guard
# publish the values it exists to protect.
tools/needles.local.json
